+# Garage-quality rivalry podium — 14 October 2026
+
+The owner rejects the flat finish and pale border, supplies Garage-versus-podium crops, and requests a 180° turn so the cars face the viewer. **RPP01** Garage-quality finish; **RPP02** clean transparent edges; **RPP03** front-facing pose; **RPP04** displayed-pixel rendering; **RPP05** bounded rendering and retained appearance. RPC01–RPC04 / RPS01 / V03–V06 / R01 / Q01 remain.
+
+The final podium uses the existing simpler meshes with the **production Garage lighting**: the same shared sky radiance, ambient colour/energy, key/fill/rim transforms, light colours/energy and original self-shadow configuration. `GarageEnvironment.build_lighting` extracts the original lighting block; ordinary Garage construction calls it with the original arguments and values. Podium chooses its transparent background. The Compact retains its exact original paint roughness, metal/specular/clearcoat and livery shaders; glazing uses the existing `ShowroomStudio._studio_glass` helper. The four other chassis originally disable paint reflections, so their podium-owned paint copies use the Compact's existing `CompactFinish.paint` profile. Their source materials and ordinary Garage/race presentation remain intact.
+
+Cars turn exactly PI radians before construction. A perspective camera retains the previous cutout framing and view direction, making the front visible without changing layout. Saved paint roles, wrap/sticker transforms and fitted part IDs remain; no uploaded condition is introduced. Awards keep their earlier detailed model, original pose, lighting and composite defaults.
+
+The old texture resolution was derived from layout units. Podium now uses the **same stretch/screen-transform calculation as CarShowroom**, at twice displayed pixel density with the Garage's four-sample 3D MSAA. Each target is capped at 1536×768 while preserving aspect. A native 2.5× scale fixture proves a logical 120×64 pane renders at 600×320 rather than enlarging a small texture.
+
+Both tested renderers retain white RGB under zero alpha (`ffffff00`). `rivalry_car_composite.gdshader` removes that matte before interpolation, composites premultiplied coverage, and respects inherited canvas tint/opacity. Partially covered MSAA silhouette pixels use an opaque colour within one source texel; transparent shadows use renderer-appropriate resolve conversion. The footprint is bounded, opaque source colours stay unchanged, and no extra geometry/image asset is added. A controlled unshaded green silhouette against navy produces **zero pale-fringe pixels** across 461 Compatibility /504 Mobile edge pixels. This is a rendered-pixel test, not only a material-property assertion. Godot's [transparent viewport tutorial](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/shaders/using_viewport_as_texture.html) informed the premultiplied composite; the clear-matte and MSAA behavior were measured in the actual pinned renderers.
+
+The preview makes three bounded first-draw refreshes so shared radiance is ready, then freezes. Weak preparation references safely handle closing/hiding the pane. Final settled menu work is 141 draw calls; deliberately forcing all three native car targets to render continuously raises that to 515, then restoring one-shot mode returns to 141. These desktop counts do not establish phone performance; initial preparation now pays higher resolution/antialiasing/shadow cost.
+
+Native evidence includes the actual [Garage-versus-podium comparison](evidence/rivalry-podium-polish-2026-10-14/gl_compatibility/quality/garage-versus-podium.png), [Mobile comparison](evidence/rivalry-podium-polish-2026-10-14/mobile/quality/garage-versus-podium.png), [small hub](evidence/rivalry-podium-polish-2026-10-14/gl_compatibility/hub-960x540.png) and [Mobile hub](evidence/rivalry-podium-polish-2026-10-14/mobile/hub-1280x720.png). The comparison uses the same explicit pink/cream striped car and fitted parts in production CarShowroom and podium, with matched camera pose. It is an isolated fixture, not a live score/account or an edit of the owner's screenshots. Each renderer folder contains all five chassis and three hub widths. Quality folders retain before/after native car views, edge fixtures and measured [Compatibility](evidence/rivalry-podium-polish-2026-10-14/gl_compatibility/quality/metrics.json) /[Mobile](evidence/rivalry-podium-polish-2026-10-14/mobile/quality/metrics.json) reflection/edge/density results.
+
+Actual commands used pinned **Godot 4.7.2.stable.official.ed1daf0bf**, through `powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1`, with isolated `.tools/rivalry-podium-*-user` APPDATA. Podium captures set `BMT_RIVALRY_CARS_EVIDENCE_DIR=res://../docs/evidence/rivalry-podium-polish-2026-10-14`.
+
+| Actual test | Outcome |
+| --- | --- |
+| `-Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_rivalry_podium_quality.gd -Graphical`, Compatibility/OpenGL and Mobile/Vulkan | **54 +54 checks, zero failures**: actual Garage finish/lighting equality, four-sample MSAA, scaled pixel density, all-five reflection ablations, edge pixels and hidden/closed lifecycle. |
+| `-Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_rivalry_custom_cars.gd -Graphical`, both renderers | **163 +163 checks, zero failures**: saved cosmetics, actual simple/front-facing models, three widths, bounded targets and settled draw work. |
+| `-Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_script_parse.gd` | **765 scripts, zero failures** in the shared workspace. |
+| `-Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_garage_reflections.gd -Graphical -RenderingMethod mobile -RenderingDriver vulkan -TestArgument '--evidence-root=res://../docs/evidence/rivalry-podium-polish-2026-10-14/garage-regression'` | **25 checks, zero failures**; actual deck14,014/floor25,343 reflection pixels and retained Garage lifecycle. |
+| `-Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_weekly_rivalry.gd -Graphical -RenderingMethod mobile -RenderingDriver vulkan` | **1,136 checks, zero failures** on the final full-app path, including navigation, three layouts and scrolling. Compatibility also passed1,136 during refinement. |
+
+Reflection ablation disables only environment reflection and compares opaque car pixels. Final mean summed RGB-byte deltas range 2.46–7.48 in Compatibility /10.98–20.76 in Mobile across the five vehicles, proving reflection contribution. The Compact comparison also checks original pigment/roughness/metal/specular/clearcoat equality and identical Garage light transforms, shadow flags and shared sky.
+
+Initial development trials exposed a white zero-alpha rectangle with naive premultiplied blending, a shader helper's invalid access to TEXTURE, nonreflective legacy paint on other chassis and a missing-metadata lookup. These were corrected. Restoring Garage MSAA exposed Mobile's linear-light matte fringe (303 pixels); conversion alone left91, and bounded interior-colour resolve removes it without loosening the edge assertion. Earlier bespoke material/light values were replaced after the owner's Garage comparison; the final Compact uses original Garage finishes. No failing invariant was weakened and no unrelated model assets were regenerated.
+
+Changed files: `game/ui/rivalry_victory_car.gd`, `weekly_rivalry_page.gd`, the extracted lighting function in `garage_environment.gd`, new `rivalry_podium_studio.gd` and `rivalry_car_composite.gdshader` plus their UIDs, extended `game/tests/test_rivalry_custom_cars.gd`, new `test_rivalry_podium_quality.gd`, this report and the RPP01–RPP05 override/status entries. The [task-only patch](evidence/rivalry-podium-polish-2026-10-14/scoped-change.patch) and receipt preserve before files and a separate Git checkpoint under `build/rivalry-podium-polish-checkpoint`; the main index and concurrent changes remain.
+
+No physical-phone test/attachment check, APK export/install, backend/canonical change, production deployment or full Validate was performed. Owner visual acceptance, phone readability/frame pacing and the previously required matching client/backend rollout for shared appearances remain. AAA is the quality target, not an automated certification.
